	The subroutines in this directory
	solve the following problem:
	\hat{g} = \arg \min_g \sum_{n=1}^N \| y_n - h(g(t_n)) \|^2 + 
	\sum_{m=1}^M \int \ddot{g}^2 dt.
	This is a penalized maximum likelihood problem,
	and it reverts to the ordinary MLE when alpha==0.
	However, since the vector spline smoothing subroutine
	called below actually uses Nexp(alpha) for alpha,
	if the MLE is desired, then set alpha to be NULL.
	The function "h" is effected by the procedure (*sigjac)(),
	that must have the following declaration:

	void sigjacfunc(out, sig, jac, off, state, sigarg)
	SIGJAC_RETURN *out;
	SIGNAL_SET sig;
	JACOB_SET jac;
	OFFSET_SET off;
	PARAM_SET state;
	Void *sigarg;

	sigarg is some structure of other possibly useful info
	that is never used anywhere but in sigjacfunc.
